---
---
<section id="transport" class="py-20 md:py-28 bg-white">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 pb-1">Getting around Yunnan</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-500 text-lg mt-4 leading-relaxed">High-speed trains connect the northwest corridor. For the south, fly or take the bus. Here is the real logistics.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 p-6 md:p-10 mb-12">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8">Northwest Corridor (Train Route)</h3>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 md:gap-4 overflow-x-auto pb-4">
        {[
          { city: "Kunming", alt: "1,890m", color: "bg-green-500" },
          { label: "2h | CNY 150", type: "arrow" },
          { city: "Dali", alt: "2,000m", color: "bg-blue-500" },
          { label: "1.5h | CNY 70", type: "arrow" },
          { city: "Lijiang", alt: "2,400m", color: "bg-purple-500" },
          { label: "1h 15min | CNY 145", type: "arrow" },
          { city: "Shangri-La", alt: "3,400m", color: "bg-red-500" },
        ].map((item) => (
          "city" in item ? (
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 bg-gray-50 rounded-xl px-4 py-3 border border-gray-100 shrink-0">
              <div class={`w-3 h-3 rounded-full ${item.color}`}></div>
              <div><div class="font-semibold text-sm text-gray-900">{item.city}</div><div class="text-xs text-gray-400">{item.alt}</div></div>
            </div>
          ) : (
            <div class="flex flex-col items-center text-xs text-gray-400 font-medium shrink-0"><div class="w-px h-4 bg-gray-300"></div><span>{item.label}</span><div class="w-px h-4 bg-gray-300"></div></div>
          )
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      {[
        { title: "Trains", desc: "The northwest corridor has excellent high-speed trains. Buy tickets on Trip.com or 12306 (foreign passport registration available).", tips: ["Trip.com is foreigner-friendly", "Book 1-2 days ahead", "Kunming has 2 stations - check which one"] },
        { title: "Flights", desc: "Flights from Kunming reach most airports in 1 hour. Best for jumping between northwest and south (Xishuangbanna).", tips: ["China Eastern hub at Kunming", "CNY 400-900 for domestic hops", "Arrive 1.5h before departure"] },
        { title: "Buses", desc: "Buses fill gaps where trains do not run. Essential for Yuanyang and rural areas. Guesthouse owners can help you find the right bus station.", tips: ["CNY 30-200 per segment", "Long-distance buses have AC", "Rarely need advance booking"] },
      ].map((item) => (
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 p-6 hover:border-gray-300 transition-colors">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">{item.title}</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">{item.desc}</p>
          <ul class="space-y-1">{item.tips.map((tip) => (<li class="text-xs text-gray-400 flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-brand-500 mt-0.5">/</span> {tip}</li>))}</ul>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="py-20 md:py-28 bg-brand-50">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-brand-200 p-8 md:p-12">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-8">
        <div class="lg:col-span-3">
          <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-brand-600 uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">Backpacker Route</div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 pb-1 mb-4">China-Laos Railway: Enter Yunnan by Train from Southeast Asia</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-6">Since 2023, the China-Laos Railway connects Kunming directly to Luang Prabang and Vientiane. This is the easiest overland route between China and Southeast Asia and it fundamentally changes how backpackers approach Yunnan.</p>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mb-6">
            {[
              { label: "Kunming to Vientiane", val: "~10 hours" },
              { label: "Kunming to Luang Prabang", val: "~7.5 hours" },
              { label: "Second class seat", val: "CNY 360-550" },
              { label: "First class sleeper", val: "CNY 700-950" },
            ].map((item) => (
              <div class="text-center p-3 rounded-xl bg-brand-50">
                <div class="text-xs text-brand-600 mb-1">{item.label}</div>
                <div class="font-bold text-gray-900">{item.val}</div>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">The train crosses the border at Mohan (China) / Boten (Laos). You will need a Lao visa (available on arrival for most nationalities, USD 40, bring passport photos). Chinese exit formalities are handled at the station. The whole border process takes about 2 hours total.</p>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs bg-brand-100 text-brand-700 px-3 py-1 rounded-full font-medium">Vientiane to Kunming: CNY 550</span>
            <span class="text-xs bg-brand-100 text-brand-700 px-3 py-1 rounded-full font-medium">Book on Trip.com or 12306</span>
            <span class="text-xs bg-brand-100 text-brand-700 px-3 py-1 rounded-full font-medium">Visa on arrival at Boten</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="lg:col-span-2">
          <div class="rounded-xl bg-gray-50 p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <div class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Why this matters for backpackers</div>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-gray-500">
              <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-500 font-bold shrink-0">1</span> Instead of flying Bangkok to Kunming, you can now train from Chiang Mai (bus to Luang Prabang, then train to Kunming) for a fraction of the cost and a much better story.</li>
              <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-500 font-bold shrink-0">2</span> The reverse route is even better: finish your Yunnan trip by taking the train south into Laos, connecting to the Southeast Asia backpacker trail without a flight.</li>
              <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-500 font-bold shrink-0">3</span> The train itself is modern Chinese high-speed rail, comfortable, and punctual. It feels nothing like the 24-hour bus journeys that used to define this route.</li>
              <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-brand-500 font-bold shrink-0">4</span> Luang Prabang is now a viable weekend trip from Kunming. You can leave Friday evening and be back by Sunday night.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
